    sh:description "ScopeExpression, is a provenanced boolean expression over scope terms that declares the applicability scope of a rule, used for composing scope dimensions with conjunction, disjunction, and exception instead of a flat single-dimension scope. A scope expression lets a rule apply to, for example, a trading session and an instrument class except a named set of instruments.";
